{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101915","id":2292398964,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6Iozt0","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101915","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101915.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101915.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101915","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101915/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101915/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101915/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/6fb169f71ce61de27bc1275e04f844280bcce037","number":101915,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Add a way to filter neighbor points to `AStar2D/3D`","user":{"login":"Chaosus","id":3036176,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzYxNzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3036176?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus","html_url":"https://github.com/Chaosus","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This PR provides a way for user to control which point needs to be processed or skipped by AStar2D/3D classes.\r\nThis can be used for various effects, including simulation of `DiagonalMode` from `AStarGrid2D`.\r\n\r\nFor example, if that AStar2D represents a 2D grid of the 256x256 dimension, the solution to orthogonal movement would look like this:\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\nextends AStar2D\r\nclass_name AStarTest\r\n\r\nvar size = 256 # use your array dimension\r\n\r\nfunc _filter_neighbor(from_id: int, neighbor_id: int) -> bool:\r\n\tvar fx = from_id % size\r\n\tvar fy = from_id / size\r\n\t\r\n\tvar nx = neighbor_id % size\r\n\tvar ny = neighbor_id / size\r\n\t\r\n\tif fx == nx || fy == ny: # only orthogonal movement is enabled (even if diagonals are connected).\r\n\t\treturn false # allow this point\r\n\t\r\n\treturn true # skip this point\r\n```\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1007033697,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMDA3MDMzNjk3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/salvageable","name":"salvageable","description":"","color":"ff7766","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1752040694,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNzUyMDQwNjk0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:navigation","name":"topic:navigation","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2025-01-22T14:35:23Z","updated_at":"2025-05-02T10:41:59Z","closed_at":"2025-05-02T08:18:42Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"abc2e4453e29dffa77faaeeee8132f38411eb13a","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"reque